{"diagnosis": "Fetch makes no progress with max_addr stuck at 0x00000000 and TRAP no progress. In mem_state 0 (picorv32.v:584) mem_valid is driven to mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word instead of its negation, so normal fetches never assert mem_valid and no transfer occurs. This contradicts the state-1 check at picorv32.v:598 mem_valid == !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word and stalls the core in fetch-highword.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -582,6 +582,6 @@
 				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
-						mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
+						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
 						mem_wstrb <= 0;
 						mem_state <= 1;
", "expected": "tohost: PASS, no TRAP, max_addr progress >0x00000000"}

